, 1132, 1045, 765, 654], "window": [3683, 42083], "confidence": 0.93, "evidence": [{"trace_id": "step_02", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_03", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_15", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_16", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_20", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_12", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_19", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_06", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_13", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_10", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_04", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_17", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_18", "role": "confounder_control"}], "narrative": "A time-ignoring path from 1885 to 1460 exists through hub 1132 and 1045, but no time-respecting sequence does. 1885's only outgoing interaction (to 1572) comes after 1572's only outgoing interaction (to 826), so the forward temporal cone of 1885 contains just 2 nodes even with unlimited waiting; under the 600-unit constraint it is likewise empty of 1460, and no temporal paths are returned. The apparent connection is an artifact of hub popularity and aggregate volume, not of ordered timing."}, "raw_final_response": "**Findings:**\n\n- Static connectivity exists: 1885\u20131132 and 1132\u20131045\u20131460 (steps 06, 13), so ignoring time there *is* a path.\n- But temporally, 1885's forward reachable set is only 2 nodes even with **no** waiting-time constraint (steps 03, 16, 20) \u2014 its outgoing event (1885\u21921572, single event, step 12) occurs after 1572's only outgoing event (1572\u2192826, step 19), so the chain dies immediately.\n- With the required max_wait = 600 the result is likewise unreachable (step 02), and no time-respecting routes exist at all (step 15).\n- Volume/popularity confounder: 1885 has just 4 events and 1460 just 3 (step 04); the high-degree hubs 1132 (162 events) and 654 (40) that make the static path look plausible are not usable in time order (steps 10, 20).\n- Activity of 1460 concentrates in bins ending \u226427682 while 1885's outbound activity is later (steps 17, 18) \u2014 timing is inverted relative to a cascade.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_9cf28e7b\",\n  \"decision\": \"absent\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"cascade\",\n  \"entities\": [1885, 1460, 1572, 1132, 1045, 765, 654],\n  \"window\": [3683, 42083],\n  \"confidence\": 0.93,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_02\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_15\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_16\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_20\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_12\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_19\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_06\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_13\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_10\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_04\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_17\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_18\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"A time-ignoring path from 1885 to 1460 exists through hub 1132 and 1045, but no time-respecting sequence does. 1885's only outgoing interaction (to 1572) comes after 1572's only outgoing interaction (to 826), so the forward temporal cone of 1885 contains just 2 nodes even with unlimited waiting; under the 600-unit constraint it is likewise empty of 1460, and no temporal paths are returned. The apparent connection is an artifact of hub popularity and aggregate volume, not of ordered timing.\"\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 69559, "total_output_tokens": 4670, "total_tokens": 74229, "total_latency_ms": 67313, "llm_calls": 9, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}